{"clock":1,"nonce":"200b960bf5976769b999b7f9cf333319","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792492153,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5940095087"},"data":{"body":"Raised in GB-17 (2026-10-19).\n\n## Kinds of release\n\n`[release]` knows one kind today: a web app (frontend, backend, admin images, maybe a Helm chart) deployed through GitOps overlays. Others we ship:\n\n- **Libraries**, published to a package registry: npm, PyPI, crates.io, …\n- **Versioned code or scripts**: the tag is the release, nothing is built.\n- **Binaries** (git-bug, git-board): built per platform and attached to the release.\n\nWhat GB-17 already covers:\n- A single-environment app cuts finals of what it runs and deploys nowhere: close to \"just push tags\".\n- `release cut --offline --no-deploy` keeps the tag local; the next online command pushes it, then builds and records it.\n\nOpen:\n- An artifact kind per `[release]` entry (image, chart, package, binary), each with a build step and a publish step.\n- Build while offline, publish once online, the same way the offline tag waits (today an offline cut defers the build as well as the push).\n\n## What still ties us to GitHub\n\nGo through each, and say where git-board stands and what is missing:\n\n1. Issues: git-bug, `refs/bugs`, with the bridge.\n2. Projects: the board.\n3. Releases: `refs/releases` and the tags (GB-17).\n4. CI/CD\n5. Code review (and Copilot review)\n6. Community: pull requests, merge requests, forks\n7. Rights and permissions\n8. Anything else?","title":"release: kinds of release beyond images and a chart, and what still ties us to GitHub"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611696,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5940095087"},"data":{"add":["kind:feat","status:backlog","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792504203,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6292426303"},"data":{"body":"Update from GB-19 (2026-10-20): **binaries** land first, as three `[release]` keys rather than a kind per entry:\n\n- `binaries = [\"./cmd/git-board\"]`, `platforms = [...]` (default: the five of `make dist`), optional `build = \"make dist\"`.\n- A table with binaries and no environments is enabled: finals only, deployed nowhere, the single-environment rules of GB-17 reused.\n- Built in a clean checkout of the tag, published with `gh release create` once the tag is pushed, recorded as `assets` (name, sha256) on the release record.\n\nStill open here:\n- The artifact kind per entry (image, chart, package, binary): GB-19's keys are what a binary entry would carry, so they move into it without a rewrite. Libraries and tag-only releases wait for it.\n- Build offline, publish online: a binaries cut made offline builds and publishes when the pending tag is pushed, like the images today. Building ahead is not done.\n- Releases on GitLab and Gitea: the Enable panel says \"GitHub only, for now\" on such a remote. Item 3 of \"What still ties us to GitHub\" now has a second tie: the forge release itself, through `gh`."}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792611696,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6324928279"},"data":{"body":"**Binaries** have shipped, now proved live: git-board v0.9.0 was cut from its own Releases page on 2026-10-21 (tag on f407a5c), with 5 archives and `checksums.txt` on the GitHub release. GB-19 is closed.\n\nFrom that cut: the build runs in a clean checkout with nothing installed, and the tag is pushed before the build. Filed as its own bug: \"release: a binary build that fails in the cut's clean checkout, after the tag is pushed\". To install a release locally: `make install-latest`.\n\nStill open here, unchanged: the artifact kind per entry (libraries, tag-only releases), building offline, and releases on GitLab and Gitea."}}]}